    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup centers around **Taylor Ward** (71.19) and **Cal Raleigh** (65.68), our two most potent options for the slate. **Taylor Ward** is an elite play, anchored by a favorable wind-aided environment and a platoon edge against Fried that pushes his efficiency well above the base projection. Meanwhile, **Cal Raleigh** benefits from a soft matchup against McCullers Jr. (4.76 xERA), allowing him to anchor the lineup despite the inherent volatility of the catcher position. **Bryson Stott** (63.92) and **Tyler Freeman** (62.02) also earn strong starts, with **Bryson Stott** leveraging a high-ceiling park and wind boost to overcome a moderately tough opposing starter, while **Tyler Freeman** remains in the mix due to his optimal spot in the order and a favorable park profile.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today's card was bypassing **Matt Chapman** (43.49), who sits just outside the core. While **Matt Chapman** presents a respectable floor, he was edged out by the superior platoon and order-dependent efficiency of **Jonathan Aranda** (52.29) and **Masyn Winn** (54.52). Despite the scarcity of stolen bases, which normally would elevate a player like **Masyn Winn**, the decision ultimately hinged on the cumulative projected run-scoring potential of our 3-hole hitters. We are exercising caution with our exposure to Ohtani; both **Luis Arraez** (47.91) and **Jung Hoo Lee** (48.85) remain active to chase contact and speed, but their scores are significantly suppressed by the 2.75 xERA they are facing. We are monitoring **Daulton Varsho** (48.10) closely, as his output remains precarious against a strong arm like Jax, though his potential to contribute to our stolen base needs provides enough utility to justify his presence in the bottom of the order.",
